    "background_story": "Xyla was a brilliant and ambitious astronaut on a mission to explore the distant planet of Xylophia-IV. As the lead navigator, she was responsible for plotting the spacecraft's trajectory. However, in her haste to reach the planet's surface, Xyla made a critical error, miscalculating the gravitational pull of the planet's moon. The mistake sent the spacecraft off course, putting the entire crew in danger. Xyla's quick thinking and expertise ultimately saved the mission, but the close call served as a humbling reminder of the importance of double-checking calculations in the high-stakes world of space exploration. Despite the setback, Xyla's reputation as a skilled astronaut remained intact, and she continued to push the boundaries of space travel.",
